      <span class="eyebrow">What Are Zygomatic Implants?</span>
      <h2 id="what-heading">A Solution for Severe Upper-Jaw Bone Loss</h2>
      <span class="gold-rule"></span>
      <p>Standard implants require adequate jawbone volume. When the upper jaw has suffered severe bone loss — due to long-term denture wear, failed previous implants, or prolonged tooth loss — conventional implants may not be possible without extensive grafting.</p>
      <p>Zygomatic implants bypass this limitation. Longer than standard implants, they anchor in the zygomatic bone (cheekbone), which retains its density regardless of what has happened to the jaw. This allows full-arch restoration in patients who might otherwise be told they are not implant candidates.</p>
    </div>
