      <span class="eyebrow">Who Is This For?</span>
      <h2 id="who-heading" class="section-heading">Patients Who Were Told No</h2>
      <span class="gold-rule"></span>
      <p>Zygomatic implants are appropriate for patients with severe maxillary (upper jaw) atrophy who need full upper-arch restoration. They may be an alternative to — or used in combination with — extensive bone grafting, sinus lifts, or other reconstructive procedures.</p>
      <p>Not every patient with upper-jaw bone loss needs zygomatic implants. A thorough imaging evaluation with {{ site.doctorName }} determines whether this approach, standard implants with grafting, or another solution is the right fit.</p>
    </div>
